     |        N  I  M         I  n  s  t  r  u  c  t  i  o  n  s         | ##
     |                                                                   | ##
     +-------------------------------------------------------------------+ ##
     |  There's really not all that much game-play in Nim; the challenge | ##
     | is to out-wit your opponent! Both players start with a pile of 17 | ##
     | objects, and alternate turns removing from that pile. On each     | ##
     | turn you may remove 1, 2 or 3 objects from the pile. The player   | ##
     | who is forced to take the last object LOSES the game!             | ##
     |                                                                   | ##
     |  Nim never gets down to this logical conclusion, however, as when | ##
     | it comes down to the wire, your opponent may simply never take    | ##
     | his or her next go! So all you have to really do is leave 1 object| ##
     | in the pile and you will WIN!                                     | ##
     |                                                   (continued...)  | ##
